  "question": {
    "text": "If the numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>a</mtext><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>14,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>a</mtext></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are the first three terms of an arithmetic progression, then its fifth term is equal to"
